    {
      "templateId": "@one-a-day/social/testimonial-proof-card/v1",
      "convention": "canvasFill",
      "severity": "error",
      "violations": [
        {
          "key": "source[0]",
          "detail": "source 0 is a static #e8eee9 fill covering the whole 1080×1080 canvas and no prop is bound to it — set document.backgroundColor instead and drop the source, or make the rect a handle (bindProp(src, \"<the prop it should edit>\") — a card bound to the theme preset is where the theme gets changed). A base rect nothing binds is a click target over everything: in Make it is selected whenever the pointer is not on a smaller tile, and the click does nothing. (A template whose SUBJECT is that rect declares it: canvas.baseRect = \"<why>\". A template that must ship it because it is composed INTO another uses defaultProps.useNestedBackgroundColor = true instead.)"
        }
      ],
      "fix": "fill the canvas with document.backgroundColor, never a full-canvas colour rect that nothing binds. A base rect is a click target that covers everything — it gets selected in Make any time the pointer is not on a smaller tile — and if no prop is bound to it that click does nothing; the document background does the same job with no rect at all. Only a STATIC, fully opaque fill counts: a curtain wipe (overlay.enable / window), a scrim (overlay.alpha) and a masked shape are legitimate and never flagged — a ROUNDED or stroked card is NOT exempt from 0.3.1 on (its corners do not change what a click on it does — a repo held to 0.3.0 keeps the exemption it shipped under), but a full-canvas rect that CARRIES A HANDLE is (a card bound to the theme preset is where the theme gets changed). Two declared exceptions, and they mean different things: canvas.baseRect = \"<why>\" is the general one (the rect IS the subject — a lesson about full-rect nodes, a tutorial surface), and defaultProps.useNestedBackgroundColor = true is the narrow one (this template is COMPOSED INTO another, whose slot its own backgroundColor cannot fill). An empty baseRect reason is refused."
    },
